Step 0 rejects this paper; no compliant generator was created.

The paper proves a decomposition for one fixed 36-variable ideal, with no scalable parameterized analogue. Its second component requires a roughly 384,000-character generator list, while verifying primariness and ideal equality entails the same Gröbner/saturation machinery used in the paper.

Track B was considered: symmetry reduces one saturation from almost 500 hours to about 10 symbolic actions, but it does not produce or certify the full decomposition. The remaining necessary computation includes a reported 117-hour saturation.

The complete, reviewable assessment is in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1811.09530/REJECTED.md), based on the [full arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1811.09530).
